From ada662a5f8f333fdd9feae7395f525fb89a85a5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "xiu.yang" <xiu.yang@sophgo.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:42:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(fip): export ENABLE_BOOTLOGO to the fsbl build

[description ]:
- scripts/fip_v2.mk: export ENABLE_BOOTLOGO (from envsetup_soc.sh, with
  ':=' to avoid make self-reference) to the fsbl make so fsbl can decide
  whether to load the boot logo partition. Pairs with the fsbl change
  that defines FSBL_LOAD_BOOTLOGO only when ENABLE_BOOTLOGO=1.

[root   cause]:
- ENABLE_BOOTLOGO only toggled U-Boot CONFIG_BOOTLOGO; fsbl never saw it
  and loaded the MISC (logo) partition unconditionally. On BF01
  (ENABLE_BOOTLOGO=0, SPI NAND, 384KB MISC) that is 192 wasted page
  reads (~30-40ms) before releasing the C906L core.

[JIRA      ID]:TBD-BF01-BOOTTIME (to be provided)
[chip project]:181x
[side effects]:
- Boards with ENABLE_BOOTLOGO=1 are unchanged (fsbl still loads the logo).
- Boards with ENABLE_BOOTLOGO=0 stop loading the logo partition in fsbl
  once the matching fsbl change is applied; U-Boot does not read the
  logo in that configuration either, so nothing consumes it.
- Verified on cv1815ja_bf01_spinand: release_blcp_2nd 363ms -> 331ms,
  AliOS media init and boot capture OK.

[Affected *.ko/*.so/*.a] :fip.bin / fip_spl.bin via fsbl define; no .ko/.so/.a

Change-Id: Ia439b2b5e83603e861646177afdd4725bb10e05a
---
 scripts/fip_v2.mk | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/scripts/fip_v2.mk b/scripts/fip_v2.mk
index 32c87dc292e2b5b0afe7c61f5135b64ec9d8c3a6..ea3ecabdc08b33fd0d8f217fdb30b268968b5f67 100644
--- a/scripts/fip_v2.mk
+++ b/scripts/fip_v2.mk
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@ fsbl%: export RTOS_FAST_IMAGE_TYPE=${CONFIG_FAST_IMAGE_TYPE}
 fsbl%: export RTOS_ENABLE_FREERTOS=${CONFIG_ENABLE_FREERTOS}
 fsbl%: export COMPRESS_RTOS_BIN=${CONFIG_COMPRESS_RTOS_BIN}
 fsbl%: export CONFIG_MIRROR_2ND_PACK_HEAD:=${CONFIG_MIRROR_2ND_PACK_HEAD}
+fsbl%: export ENABLE_BOOTLOGO:=${ENABLE_BOOTLOGO}
 endif
 fsbl%: export FSBL_SECURE_BOOT_SUPPORT=${CONFIG_FSBL_SECURE_BOOT_SUPPORT}
 fsbl%: export ARCH=$(call qstrip,${CONFIG_ARCH})
-- 
